---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "King Cole Bar",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Bar Food", "Cocktails"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-212-339-6857",
  url: "https://www.kingcolebar.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "2 E 55th St",
    addressLocality: "New York",
    addressRegion: "NY",
    postalCode: "10022",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Historic cocktail bar inside The St. Regis New York, birthplace of the Bloody Mary (created here in 1934 as the 'Red Snapper').",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="King Cole Bar Menu Guide — Bloody Mary Birthplace, NYC"
  description="Independent guide to King Cole Bar at the St. Regis New York: the famous Red Snapper Bloody Mary ($25), signature cocktails, bar bites with reported prices, history, and visiting tips. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/king-cole-bar-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/king-cole-bar.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/king-cole-bar.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a historic 1930s hotel cocktail bar with a large mural — an artist's interpretation, not the actual King Cole Bar"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Midtown · The St. Regis
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      King Cole Bar — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Inside The St. Regis New York at 2 East 55th Street sits one of the most storied bars
      in cocktail history. This is where the Bloody Mary was born — in 1934, French bartender
      Fernand Petiot mixed vodka with tomato juice and called it the Red Snapper, because
      "Bloody Mary" was considered too vulgar for such an elegant room. Below is our independent
      walkthrough of the drinks menu, reported prices, and how to do the visit justice. Everything
      is written in our own words; prices are reported figures, not a copy of the bar's menu.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">2 E 55th St, New York, NY 10022 (inside The St. Regis)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Known for</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Birthplace of the Bloody Mary (1934); Maxfield Parrish's "Old King Cole" mural</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Classic American bar — cocktails and bar bites</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Cocktails reported ~$24–30; the Red Snapper ~$25</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported: Mon–Sat 11:30am–midnight; Sun noon–midnight</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (212) 339-6857</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The Red Snapper &amp; the Bloody Mary selection</h2>
      <p>
        This is why you come. The bar offers a Bloody Mary selection reported at <strong>$25</strong>,
        built around the original Red Snapper — Belvedere vodka, tomato juice, lemon juice and spices,
        served in a wine glass rather than the usual tumbler. The rest of the selection riffs on the
        theme, each named for a different St. Regis property around the world.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Drink</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Red Snapper — the original 1934 Bloody Mary, St. Regis New York</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Bloody Smoke — scotch-based, celery, olives, cracked pepper</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Harry's Texas Bloody Mary — tequila with Cajun seasoning</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">The Capitol Mary — gin with Old Bay seasoning, oyster crackers</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Agave Maria — tequila, green jalapeño garnish</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">The Mary Terranean — vodka with olive oil, basil and oregano</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">~$25</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        A caveat: published sources list the $25 figure for the selection as a whole, and individual
        preparations may vary in price. Ask your server before ordering if the exact figure matters to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature cocktails</h2>
      <p>
        Beyond the Marys, the cocktail list is a greatest-hits of Midtown classics, mostly reported
        at <strong>$24</strong>, with one premium pour at $30. The names themselves are a tour of the
        neighborhood and the hotel's history.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Cocktail</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Fifth And 55th — vodka, lime, cherry preserves (the house premium)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$30</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Old King Cole — gin, vermouth, amaro, burnt orange</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">The Maxfield Parrish — rum-based, amaro, vermouth, bitters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Astor Midnight — blueberry vodka, lavender, sparkling wine</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Best Address — reposado tequila, ginger liqueur, lemon, sriracha bitters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Madison Avenue — tequila, lime, blood orange soda, salt</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">1904 — whiskey, lemon, sage (a nod to the hotel's founding year)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Midtown Spice — bourbon, apple liqueur, ginger, cherry</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$24</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Bar bites</h2>
      <p>
        This is a bar, not a restaurant — the food list is short and built for drinking alongside.
        Reported prices run from <strong>$8 to $26</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Bite</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Grilled lamb merguez with roasted grapes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$26</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">"Nizza" spicy eggplant with goat cheese</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$15</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Mediterranean olives</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$9</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Fried chichi's (chickpea fritters)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$8</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>The Red Snapper is non-negotiable — it's the whole point of the pilgrimage:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The ritual:</strong> the Red Snapper, in the wine glass, under the mural. Order it first.</li>
        <li><strong>The second round:</strong> the Old King Cole — a proper gin drink named for the room itself.</li>
        <li><strong>With it:</strong> the lamb merguez, the one substantial bite on the menu, built for a second drink.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Look up.</strong> The Maxfield Parrish "Old King Cole" mural (1904) dominates the room — it's the visual centerpiece of the visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Go at golden hour.</strong> Late afternoon into early evening is when the room glows and the crowd is at its most civilized.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress smart.</strong> This is a St. Regis bar; the room expects you to make an effort.</li>
        <li><strong>It's a drink, not dinner.</strong> Pair this with a dinner reservation elsewhere — the food menu is snacks, not a meal.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Prices above are <strong>reported as of October 2026</strong>, compiled from publicly reported
        menus and listings. Bar menus change and prices move — the Bloody Mary selection in particular
        has been listed with varying figures. Always verify current prices with the bar before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
